# Lambda runtime dependencies shared across providers. Compiled into
# requirements-{aws,alicloud}.txt by pip-compile; per-cloud .in files
# (lambda/requirements-aws.in, lambda/requirements-alicloud.in) chain
# this file via `-r requirements.in` and add the cloud-specific SDKs.
#
# This split exists because PR #84 added the alibaba SDKs
# (oss2 / alibabacloud_kms20160120 / alibabacloud_ecs20140526) for the
# BLITZLOG_PROVIDER=alicloud path. The factory in lambda/provider/
# __init__.py lazy-imports the alicloud provider, so an AWS cold start
# never loads the alibaba wheels — but `terraform apply` of
# infra/aws/dev was still bundling all of them into the AWS Lambda
# zip. PyJWT / cryptography / requests are used by both providers'
# code, so they stay here.
#
# Adding a dep:
#   * Used by every provider     -> add here.
#   * Used only by AWS           -> add to requirements-aws.in.
#   * Used only by alicloud      -> add to requirements-alicloud.in.
# Then run `mise run lock` (or the explicit pip-compile invocations
# documented in mise.toml) to regenerate both per-cloud .txt files.
PyJWT
cryptography
requests
